# Claude Code local (machine-specific) settings — never commit
.claude/settings.local.json

# Credential files that get pasted into the working tree by accident.
# This repo is PUBLIC: a stray `git add -A` would publish them instantly,
# and git history cannot be un-published. Belt and braces on top of
# keeping secrets in /etc/tickermover.env on the server.
*keys*.txt
*keys*.docx
*secret*
*credential*
api-keys*
*.env.local
# Screenshots of credential dashboards. Every rule above is extension-anchored
# to text files, so none of them matched `cloudflare API.png` — it sat
# untracked but perfectly committable in a PUBLIC repo. A token is just as live
# in a PNG as in a .txt.
*api*.png
*API*.png
*token*.png
*key*.png
